+## Front page load speed: three.js and pdf.js off the first-paint path
+
+Branch `fix/home-load-speed` (fix 3 of the 2026-11-10 global check). Measured with Lighthouse
+12.8.2 mobile on a built tree (`di-dev up --prod --api scratch`), median of 3, before then after:
+LCP 6.9 s then 3.5 s, TBT 349 then 187 ms, performance 65 then 86, 974 then 314 KiB on the wire.
+The door flight and the falling page load by `import()` when the room is wanted; pdf.js, the
+realtime client, search and QR get their own chunks. The front page chunk no longer imports
+`three-vendor`. Guard: `src/landing/landingEntryWeight.test.js`. LCP 2.5 s is not reached; the
+remainder is the MUI vendor chunk and render-blocking CSS (a product decision). No look or wording change.
